## URL Roots And Linking Rules

The URL Tool must link live online resources across different roots:
- Core app root (web):
  - Root: `https://www.noble-architecture.com/na-apps/20__PlanVision__CoreAppCode`
  - Index: `https://www.noble-architecture.com/na-apps/20__PlanVision__CoreAppCode/index.html`
- Project portal root (web):
  - Root: `https://www.noble-architecture.com/na-project-portal/`
  - Typical project:
    - `https://www.noble-architecture.com/na-project-portal/25-Projects/JH03__RomerCottage`

## URL Tool Behavior
- **Live web usage**
  - When constructing links to resources in different roots, the URL Tool must output absolute web URLs pointing to the live online versions.
  - This is required because the core app and project content live under different web roots.
**
- **Localhost usage**
  - When running locally, the URL Tool must use local relative paths instead of the live web roots.
  - Local relative paths should mirror the repo folder structure for the core app and project portal.
  This is the local path to the core app repository:
  `D:\WE10_--_Public-Repo_--_Live-Website\na-apps\20__PlanVision__CoreAppCode`
  This is the local path to the project portal repository:
  `D:\WE10_--_Public-Repo_--_Live-Website\na-project-portal`
    - Relative path to the project portal repository from the Application Shell Root:
        `../na-project-portal`
  This is a typical project folder:
  `D:\WE10_--_Public-Repo_--_Live-Website\na-project-portal\25-Projects\JH03__RomerCottage`
       - Relative path to the project folder from the Application Shell Root:
        `../na-project-portal/25-Projects/JH03__RomerCottage`

## Intent
The same link-building logic must support both:
- Live production URLs across multiple web roots.
- Local development with relative paths.